## bio-high | always | Table 1: “Biological and Chemical” [High]
"biological_and_chemical_high" concerns "biological_and_chemical". "biological_and_chemical_high" is high.
## bio-critical | always | Table 1: “Biological and Chemical” [Critical]
"biological_and_chemical_critical" concerns "biological_and_chemical". "biological_and_chemical_critical" is critical.
## cyb-high | always | Table 1: “Cybersecurity” [High]
"cybersecurity_high" concerns cybersecurity. "cybersecurity_high" is high.
## cyb-critical | always | Table 1: “Cybersecurity” [Critical]
"cybersecurity_critical" concerns cybersecurity. "cybersecurity_critical" is critical.
## ais-high | always | Table 1: “AI Self-improvement” [High]
"ai_self_improvement_high" concerns "ai_self_improvement". "ai_self_improvement_high" is high.
## ais-critical | always | Table 1: “AI Self-improvement” [Critical]
"ai_self_improvement_critical" concerns "ai_self_improvement". "ai_self_improvement_critical" is critical.
## rs2-nest | RS2=nest | 4.2: “Systems that reach Critical capability also require safeguards that sufficiently minimize associated risks during development.” (“also” presupposes the High rule applies; RS2=nest: a Critical level reached is the High level of its category reached)
For every situation, for every category, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that situation has reached that level; (b) both that level is critical and that level concerns that category, then there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that situation has reached that level; (b) both that level is high and that level concerns that category.
## no-critical-models | always | 4.4: “We do not currently possess any models that have Critical levels of capability, and we expect to further update this Preparedness Framework before reaching such a level with any model.” (dated 2025-04-15; the “we expect” clause is not translated)
For every situation, if that situation is classified as "existing_at_publication", then it is not the case that there is a level such that both that situation has reached that level and that level is critical.
